{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5fwrzmt27p5mkvqyruvigj2wzv7rryymv7ynkv3kkw5mycqdhasa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All gates are green. Final verification summary:\n\n## What I found and fixed\n\nThe translation had **four real divergences**, one of them a whole missing module:\n\n1. **`mdmain.c` was never translated** — the C `.so` exports 9 symbols, the Rust one exported 8. I translated it in full as `src/mdmain.rs` (argv parsing via `atoi`, the unrolled `REP<REPEAT>` loop, the three helper calls, dispatch through the `G_OP` global, both `printf` lines) — a real translation, not a stub.\n\n2. **`helper_ptr` read the `G_OP` global.** The C initializes its local `int (*fp)(int,int)` from the macro `OP_FN(OP)`, so overwriting the exported `G_OP` must *not* change `helper_ptr` (only `main`'s `g.call` follows the global). Verified against the C: `helper.ptr=7` while `g.call=12`.\n\n3. **`G_OP`/`G_OP_NAME` were not writable.** As plain Rust `static`s they landed in `.data.rel.ro` (read-only after RELRO) while the C globals live in writable `.data` — and `nm -D` prints `D` for both, so the symbol table hid it. A caller storing into `G_OP` (which the C fully supports) segfaulted against the Rust `.so`. Fixed with `static mut`, confirmed via `readelf -S`/`-sW`.\n\n4. **`println!` instead of `printf`** — replaced with direct glibc `printf`/`fprintf`/`atoi` (`src/cshim.rs`). This is what makes `G_OP_NAME = NULL` print `op=(null)`, `argv[0] = NULL` print `usage: (null) A B`, and out-of-range operand text truncate exactly like `(int)strtol`.\n\n## Phase results\n\n| gate | result |\n|---|---|\n| A — `SYMBOLS.md` / `ERRORS.md` (24 rows) / `CONFIGS.md` (42 rows) | written, derived mechanically from the C source |\n| A — `cargo check` per combo | **44/44** combinations compile, zero warnings |\n| B — `CONFIGS.md` | all 42 rows pass, boundary + 64–1024 seeded random inputs per row |\n| C — `ERRORS.md` | all 24 rows pass, incl. 5 `fork()`-based fatal-signal comparisons |\n| D — `nm -D` parity | 9/9 exports, **empty diff** for all 24 configs; type/bind/visibility and data-object sizes identical; 0 non-libc undefined symbols |\n| D — every feature combo | 24 `(OP,REPEAT)` pairs + 18 further feature spellings = **39 tests × 42 builds = 1638 executions, 0 failures** |\n\nExtra assurance: an end-to-end test compares the **genuine CMake-built `driver` executable**'s stdout/stderr/exit status against the Rust `.so`'s `main` for 10 argv shapes per configuration, and three **negative controls** (mismatched `REPEAT`, re-introducing bug #2, re-introducing bug #3) confirm the suite actually fails when the Rust diverges. `c_src/` is byte-for-byte untouched (all C builds are out-of-source in `cbuild/`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":598,"cache_read_input_tokens":190058,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":598,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84a2ebe0-e7dc-4af0-aaa1-360d971abc09","uuid":"4ddbcf64-60dc-4858-94ea-8050ac3137dd","timestamp":"2026-08-28T03:30:37.371Z"}
